<title>USA: U.S. DLA sold 200 tonnes stockpile tin.</title>
<headline>U.S. DLA sold 200 tonnes stockpile tin.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Defense Logistics Agency said Wednesday that it sold 200 tonnes of surplus longhorn tin to two firms at an average price of $2.7710 per pound.</p>
<p>DLA said it made the award to American Iron and Metal Co Inc of Montreal, Canada.</p>
<p>Spot tin is offered on the first Wednesday of each month. Since the first Wednesday in January is a holiday, the next bid opening will be January 8.</p>
